/-!
# Koszul-regularity in a pair of immersions over a locally Noetherian algebraic space

Let `i : Z ⟶ Y` and `j : Y ⟶ X` be immersions of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` with `X`
locally Noetherian.  Then the following three conditions agree:

1. `i` is a Koszul-regular immersion and `j` is one near the image of `i`,
2. `i` and `i ≫ j` are Koszul-regular immersions,
3. `i ≫ j` is a Koszul-regular immersion and the conormal sequence
   `0 ⟶ i^* 𝒞_{Y/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/Y} ⟶ 0` of Stacks tag 06BD is exact and locally split.

This is Stacks tag 09S2, whose proof in the source is "immediate from the case of schemes",
namely from Stacks tag 0690.

## The argument

Each of the three conditions is read on the étale scheme charts of `X`, which is how this
development states every condition on algebraic spaces whose scheme analogue it localizes:  the
three regularity predicates of Stacks tag 06BN, the conditions of Stacks tag 03MJ, and the
conormal hypothesis `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsSplitExactConormalSequenceOnEtaleCharts` of
Stacks tag 09S1.  Over a chart `c` of `X` the pair of scheme immersions is the base change of
`j` to `c` together with the base change of `i` to the chart of `Y` that `j` pulls back from
`c`, and those two base changes compose to the base change of `i ≫ j` up to the comparison
isomorphism of two cartesian squares — the decomposition already used for Stacks tag 09S0 in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/RegularImmersionComposition.lean`.  Being locally
Noetherian passes from the atlas witnessing it to every étale chart by Stacks tag 03E8, so each
chart of `X` is a locally Noetherian scheme and the chart of `Y` is one too, an immersion into a
locally Noetherian scheme being locally of finite type.

On a chart the three conditions are Stacks tag 0690, which this development carries pointwise
and for *regular* immersions, as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_opens_isRegularImmersion_of_split` and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_opens_isRegularImmersion_comp_of_factors`.
Two passages are therefore needed and are both supplied below for schemes.  Regularity and
Koszul-regularity agree over a locally Noetherian target, which is Stacks tag 063L.  And
regularity in a neighbourhood of *every* point of the source is global regularity:  the locus
where the kernel of the map of local rings is generated by a regular sequence is open and is
exactly the regular locus, so `isRegularImmersion_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap` turns the
pointwise statements into global ones.  The conclusion about `i` is then transported from the
charts of `Y` pulled back from `X` to all charts of `Y` by Stacks tag 06BM, as in tag 09S1.

## What is carried

Nothing is assumed that the library does not prove:  there is no extra hypothesis beyond the
source's own, and no condition of the source is dropped.  One condition is *corrected*, and the
correction is recorded in the attribute's clause string.

**Why `j` is only Koszul-regular near the image of `i`.**  Stacks tag 09S2 states condition (1)
as "`i` and `j` are Koszul-regular immersions", with no qualifier, whereas the scheme-level tag
0690 it reduces to is stated at a point of `Z`:  there, condition (1) is that `i` is a regular
immersion in a neighbourhood of `z` and `j` is one in a neighbourhood of `i z`.  The global
reading of tag 09S2 is false.  Take `Z` empty, `Y` the closed subscheme of `X = Spec k[a, b]`
cut out by `(a, b)²` — an ideal of height two needing three generators, hence generated by no
regular sequence, so `j` is not Koszul-regular by tag 063L.  Conditions (2) and (3) hold
vacuously, since both only speak about morphisms out of the empty `Z`, and condition (1) fails.
Nothing about `j` away from the image of `i` can be concluded from `i` and `i ≫ j`, and the
clause of condition (1) formalized here is the one the cited proof delivers:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsKoszulRegularImmersionNearImageOnEtaleCharts`, Koszul-regularity of
`j` on a neighbourhood of every point of the image of `i`, read on the étale charts of `X`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsKoszulRegularImmersionNearImage`:  for schemes,
  Koszul-regularity of `j` on a neighbourhood of every point of the image of `i`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsKoszulRegularImmersionNearImageOnEtaleCharts`:  the same condition
  for algebraic spaces, read on the étale scheme charts of `X`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isKoszulRegularImmersion_tfae_of_isLocallyNoetherian`:  **Stacks tag
  09S2**, the three equivalent conditions.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isKoszulRegularImmersion_comp_of_nearImage` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isKoszulRegularImmersion_and_nearImage_of_comp`:
  the two implications for schemes, in the global Koszul form that the algebraic-space statement
  consumes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 76.44.10 (Tag 09S2)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09S2)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.9 (Tag 0690)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0690)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.3 (Tag 063L)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063L)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 76.44.6 (Tag 09S1)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09S1)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 76.44.5 (Tag 09RZ)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09RZ)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 76.44.3 (Tag 06BP)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06BP)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 76.44.8 (Tag 06BM)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06BM)
